				<wikidot:authorName>dankaar</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1790336</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>Maybe because I lack the knowledge on the reference this article used..</p> </blockquote> <p>Possibly. It uses the fact that in nass media, the &quot;<a href="http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/MadScientist">Mad Scientist</a>&quot; character archetype will often create crazy experiments with a high chance of spectacularly backfiring. Some of the earliest ones in fiction were often associated with chemistry, hence the beaker.</p> <p>In short, this simply pokes fun at that character archetype.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
